  "details": "Severe case (all the items):\n\n1. Open the Players debug overlay\n\n2. Spawn a couple (dozen) items (NOT the Multiple Companion Cube)\n\n3. Watch the network \"Suffering\" indicator bounce around in single-digit range, sometimes reaching low multi-digit\n\n4. Spawn the Multiple Companion Cube item\n\n5. Watch the \"Suffering\" indicator skyrocket to >120\n\n6. Despawn the Multiple Companion Cube item\n\n7. Watch the \"Suffering\" indicator drop back down to 0 only very slowly\n\nWorst offender (just the Multiple Companion Cube item):\n\n1. Open the Players debug overlay\n\n2. Spawn only the Multiple Companion Cube item\n\n3. Watch the \"Suffering\" indicator slowly rise to ~100\n\n4. Despawn the Multiple Companion Cube item\n\n5. Watch the \"Suffering\" indicator drop back down to 0 immediately\n\nThis causes an issue where remote players that have multiple items spawned, especially the Multiple Companion Cube, will appear with a very large delay (\"Fnl D\" indicator in the player list) of ~4-5 seconds.",
